From: ps5wl contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ADT: state SmallVector element alignment on the complete class

The PS5 ABI does not propagate an over-aligned empty storage base's alignment
into the derived SmallVector<T,0>. Keep all upstream layout assertions enabled;
state both required alignments on the complete class instead. Multiple alignas
specifiers select the stricter alignment, so byte-sized elements still retain
the header's natural alignment. Ordinary host layouts remain unchanged.

--- a/llvm/include/llvm/ADT/SmallVector.h
+++ b/llvm/include/llvm/ADT/SmallVector.h
@@ -1181,4 +1181,5 @@
 template <typename T,
           unsigned N = CalculateSmallVectorDefaultInlinedElements<T>::value>
-class LLVM_GSL_OWNER SmallVector : public SmallVectorImpl<T>,
+class alignas(SmallVectorImpl<T>) alignas(T) LLVM_GSL_OWNER SmallVector
+    : public SmallVectorImpl<T>,
                                    SmallVectorStorage<T, N> {
